Count leaf nodes
A leaf has both children NULL.
int countLeaves(TreeNode* root) {
if (root == NULL) return 0;
if (root->left == NULL && root->right == NULL) return 1;
return countLeaves(root->left) + countLeaves(root->right);
}
Two base cases here. The NULL case protects against crashes, the leaf case is where the counting
actually happens. On our tree: leaves are 4, 5, 6, so the answer is 3.
A very common wrong version writes if (root->left == NULL || root->right == NULL)
