bool searchBST(TreeNode* root, int target) {
if (root == NULL) return false ;
if (root->val == target) return true ;
if (target < root->val) return searchBST(root->left, target);
return searchBST(root->right, target);
}
Now only one side is explored, so the cost is O(H): O(log N) on a balanced BST. This is the payoff for
the extra ordering promise.
Same tree
LeetCode 100. Two trees are identical if they have the same shape and the same values in the same
places.
New idea: the function takes two pointers and walks both trees in step.
bool isSameTree(TreeNode* p, TreeNode* q) {
if (p == NULL && q == NULL) return true ; // both ended together
if (p == NULL || q == NULL) return false ; // one ended first, shapes differ
if (p->val != q->val) return false ;
return isSameTree(p->left, q->left) &&
isSameTree(p->right, q->right);
}
