Read that carefully , because it contains the entire lesson of this part:
• L + R is the answer through this node. It uses both children. It is recorded, not returned.
• 1 + max(L, R) is what the parent can use. It continues through one child only .
If you ever find yourself wanting to return L + R upward, stop. That would be claiming the parent
can extend a path that already turned a corner, which is geometrically impossible.
Always reset the member variable at the start of the public function, since LeetCode reuses the object
across test cases.
